<p>First of all, thanks for the crit, now let me explain some of my thought process</p>
<p>With the symmetrical hole, I really included that as a way for the Foundation to know something was off (rather than just a non-anomalous entity making people disappear), but you're right that I should tie it in at the end. I was mostly thinking of having actual fairies manipulate the situation rather than just fairy-like, so I could have a central fairy that speaks and talks to possibly one of MTF to show that it isn't just the forest being anomalous, but it's inhabitants. I also prefer having it be fairies rather than a fairy-like forest because it gives the SCP more agency rather than just 'spooky forest make bad things happen'.</p>
<p>A tale could work, to be honest, I was more biased towards an article because I'm more familiar with them compared to tales but I'll keep it in mind.</p>

