			<div class="content" id="post-content-4843724">
									

<blockquote>
<p>And so it seems to me that stripping this right down to it's core and focussing on the impact the radio has on e.g. a d-class and like, them like, reconnecting with their grandmother and forgiving her for her mistakes in life, and then, slowly, over time, them coming to the realisation this isn't their grandmother and having the whole forgiveness thing ripped away from them again and the old wounds reopened would be a lot more effective, narratively, than this? Or like…at least having some kind of personal, emotional growth story influenced by like, the radio, y'know?</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Oh yeah, all of your aforementioned points made lots of sense. Its just that I am trying to deviate from the usual &quot;wholesome scp is beneficial, but just stays hidden forever and its full impact to other aspects wasn't explored&quot; kinda story. Yeah, I am trying to tackle two angles for this story, but I am also planning not to delve into it too much in order not to extend the article in such unholy length (since this is my first skip, and writing short ones is said to be more perfect for beginners like me). I am just gonna provide a summarized sneak peak/teaser of the full scenario of those aforementioned angles, through the addendums.</p>

